# $copyClass(pSourceRef,pTargetLibRef) — the ONE safe class-to-class copy.
# Used by both directions: backup (live -> vault) and restore (vault -> live).
# REBIRTH, always (§A8.12c): an in-place $classdata.$assign onto an EXISTING
# window class is a silent no-op — flag YES, moddate frozen. A FRESH target has
# no such wall, whatever the class type. So whatever stands at the target name
# is renamed ASIDE and kept as the net until the seal holds.
# Only $classdata travels. Measured 2026-08-31 in execScratch:
#   $userinfo TRAVELS — left alone here, it round-trips for free
#   $desc, $version, $vcsrevision, $parentfolder do NOT travel
# The CALLER puts those four back; this method never touches them.
# Seal: $sealCompare, structural per class type — class methods, variables, and the
# objects with their methods where the type has them (sealwalk v1, thread 040). A copy
# is a fresh birth and cdif can never acquit it (§A8.12d). Method text normalised for
# the requalification law on BOTH $ctask. and $cinst.
# On a failed seal the newborn goes and the net comes back: NOTHING changed.
# Returns the protocol text.
# The note does NOT name this method. It is called only from other methods,
# never from the console, so its line is always preceded by the caller's own
# name — a second prefix in front of the first is noise. Every branch ends the
# same way: a sentence, a full stop, a space, so a caller can embed it and add
# nothing. Same rule as the vault note.
If pSourceRef
Else
	Quit method 'source empty — nothing copied. '
End If
If pSourceRef.$classtype*1>0
Else
	Quit method con(chr(91),pSourceRef.$name,chr(93),' is not a class (group or object reference?) — nothing copied. ')
End If
If pTargetLibRef
Else
	Quit method 'target library empty — nothing copied. '
End If
Calculate cName as pSourceRef.$name
Calculate asideName as con(cName,'_aside')
Calculate proto as ''
# a leftover aside means an earlier run died mid-flight — say so, then clear it
If pTargetLibRef.$classes.$findname(asideName)
	Do pTargetLibRef.$classes.$remove(pTargetLibRef.$classes.$findname(asideName).$ref)
	Calculate proto as con('leftover [',asideName,'] from an earlier run removed; ')
End If
Calculate had as kFalse
If pTargetLibRef.$classes.$findname(cName)
	Set reference oldRef to pTargetLibRef.$classes.$findname(cName)
	Do oldRef.$name.$assign(asideName)
	If pTargetLibRef.$classes.$findname(asideName)
		Calculate had as kTrue
	Else
		Quit method con(proto,'could not move ',chr(91),cName,chr(93),' aside — NOTHING changed. ')
	End If
End If
Set reference tgtRef to pTargetLibRef.$classes.$add(pSourceRef.$classtype,cName)
If tgtRef
Else
	If had
		Do pTargetLibRef.$classes.$findname(asideName).$name.$assign(cName)
	End If
	Quit method con(proto,'could not create ',chr(91),cName,chr(93),' — rolled back, NOTHING changed. ')
End If
Do tgtRef.$classdata.$assign(pSourceRef.$classdata) Returns ok
# FRESH-PATH SEAL (§A8.6): never read through the add-returned reference
Set reference tgtRef to pTargetLibRef.$classes.$findname(cName)
Calculate sealText as $cinst.$sealCompare(pSourceRef,tgtRef)
Calculate ok as pos('OK',sealText)=1 ## the answer starts with OK only when every row matched
Calculate proto as con(proto,'seal ',sealText) ## keeps the token seal OK that $backupClass searches
If ok
	# who writes, saves (persistence law) — only a sealed copy earns the disk
	Save class [con(pTargetLibRef.$name,'.',cName)]
	Calculate ok as #F ## honest save flag: read straight after the save, not later
	Calculate proto as con(proto,', saved [',ok,']')
End If
If ok
	If had
		Do pTargetLibRef.$classes.$remove(pTargetLibRef.$classes.$findname(asideName).$ref)
	End If
	Quit method con(cName,' -> ',pTargetLibRef.$name,', ',proto,pick(had,', no net was needed, the target name was free',', net removed'),'. ')
Else
	# ROLLBACK — the newborn goes, the net comes back under the original name
	Do pTargetLibRef.$classes.$remove(pTargetLibRef.$classes.$findname(cName).$ref)
	If had
		Do pTargetLibRef.$classes.$findname(asideName).$name.$assign(cName)
	End If
	Quit method con(proto,' — ROLLED BACK, ',chr(91),cName,chr(93),' is as it was. ')
End If